 the first half is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paired with the k-th of the second half. Every pairing of the stubs is equally likely, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loops and parallel edges occur; a self-loop counts 2 toward its vertex’s degree, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every vertex has exactly its degree. The edges are at positions ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<m","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in pairing order,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each written (first-half end, second-half end). The shuffle is Fisher–Yates, i from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last stub down to 1 swapped with ","type":"text"},{"code":"below(i + 1)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/randomgraphs\/multigraphs\/pseudograph\/configurationmodel(degreesequence:using:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/RandomGraphs\/documentation\/RandomGraphs\/Multigraphs\/Pseudograph\/configurationModel(degreeSequence:using:)"},"doc://Multigraphs/documentation/Multigraphs/DirectedPseudograph":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedPseudograph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DirectedPseudograph","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph that allows parallel edges and self-loops."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedPseudograph","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/multigraphs\/directedpseudograph","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Multigraphs\/documentation\/Multigraphs\/DirectedPseudograph"}}}